  "trigger": "User explicitly invoked $best-api-review reads go after selecting the next queue scope.",
  "requirements": [
    "Read one coherent document/root at the proper committed or transaction-draft lifetime, preserving exact installed capabilities and pure read guards.",
    "Retain immutable historical values and node-key locations independently of live callable read topology.",
    "Publish current selector values synchronously with equality, cleanup, view retirement and native DOM-sync ordering preserved.",
    "Answer precise consumer dependencies through canonical changes without a second document or change store.",
    "Consider the strongest deletion, merge and replacement alternatives; do not adopt unmeasured runtime architecture or implement downstream product changes during review."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "First reads-scope immutable review. Rechecked the August 18 plan against current source and 19 read-view/node-key lifecycle tests; its live topology decision is reaffirmed, not treated as a hard constraint. Reconciled September 9 E06 against useGenericSelector/useNodeSelector and kept its generic-store rewrite Defer. Fresh primary-root path-membership packets and 56 focused tests support this review; older browser/performance results are not reused as current proof.",
  "summary": "Pursue precise commit-owned invalidation membership and demand-sensitive consumers: one unchanged-key query currently derives the entire shifted path set. At 8,192 paragraphs the isolated cached prototype cuts first-query index calls from 32,788 to two and retains zero repeated-read index calls. Preserve live read topology, historical snapshots, middleware and DOM-owned rendering distinctions.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": null,
  "relation": "initial",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure: retain current direct and callback read calls and configuration-scoped method topology. Caller shouldUpdate filters cannot avoid aggregation inside hasNodeKey.",
    "Change existing owner: pursue precise memoized membership on EditorCommit.changed, splitting path membership from aggregate root details. Adapt React dispatch and DOM binding demand before claiming mounted savings.",
    "Add a primitive: reject observed-read handles, automatic dependency tracking and a new signal graph for this bounded job; existing identity and change queries express the dependency.",
    "Delete/merge live views and snapshots: reject collapsing independently required historical and live/draft/root lifetimes. Rebinding all extension methods per revision restores work or another lifetime layer.",
    "Delete snapshot indexes into the token index: not justified; retained runtime identities and canonical token positions have distinct contracts, and moving their mapping does not remove the observed eager query work.",
    "Move all subscriptions to core: keep canonical model invalidation in core, with DOM text-sync suppression and mounted-view retirement in React. Do not add a core event bus for native rendering decisions.",
    "Replace generic selector store: retain prior E06 Defer; the current probe attributes commit membership, not selector-store allocation, concurrent render safety or Compiler overhead."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "56 current-source tests pass: 19 read-view/node-key, 10 middleware, 21 commit metadata and six React selectors. The prototype tests warm materialized primary-root indexes at 32/1,024/8,192 paragraphs with 0/1/32/all watchers, five alternating samples, 70 guard-key observations and exact parity. The uncached prototype is preserved and rejected for repeated-read cost. The cached isolated membership law passes, but complete React dispatch remains provisional: cold/lazy index behavior, multiple roots, all mutation kinds, retained memory, DOM bindings and native ordering need owning adoption proof. Browser specs were inspected, not run. No end-to-end latency, full scope coverage, product implementation or release claim.",
